IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-1984`
IMPORT `cat-act-facts`
IMPORT `cat-regulations-2012`
IMPORT `part-1-preliminary`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA), compilation 00-l0-01, currency start 25 Sep 2025 (mrdoc_48898).
-- Part 2 Division 5 -- Changes to recorded information: s 25. LQA run cat-act-2011-lqa,
-- step 4A, 2026-10-01.

§ `Section 25 -- Notice to be given of changes to recorded information`

-- s 25: "The owner of a cat must give notice in writing — (a) to the local government with which
-- the cat is registered, if there is a change to any of the information prescribed under section
-- 12(3) in respect of the cat; and (b) to the microchip database company for that cat, if there
-- is a change to any of the information prescribed under section 15 in respect of the cat,
-- within 7 days after the change to the information. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
-- The information: Cat Regulations r 16 for (a), r 17 for (b). The owner is the owner on the
-- day of the change.

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25(a); Cat Regulations 2012 r 16
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, i IS AN `Information item`, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(a) -- the duty applies to` o `for` c `on a change to` i `on` d IF
        "The owner of a cat" ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` d
    ... "to the local government with which the cat is registered" ... `s 3(1) --` c `is registered on` d
    ... "a change to any of the information prescribed under section 12(3)"
        ... i `is an item among` `r 16 -- the information prescribed under s 12(3)`

-- FORK-15, reading A (taken): the information "prescribed under section 15" is what the
-- implanter gives under s 15 as at implanting. The cat's age is fixed by that; it does not
-- "change" as the cat grows older.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25(b); Cat Regulations 2012 r 17 (FORK-15 reading A)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, i IS AN `Information item`, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(b) -- the duty applies to` o `for` c `on a change to` i `on` d IF
        "The owner of a cat" ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` d
    ... "to the microchip database company for that cat" ... `s 3(1) -- there is a microchip database company for` c
    ... "a change to any of the information prescribed under section 15"
        ... i `is an item among` `r 17 -- the information prescribed under s 15`
        ... NOT i EQUALS `the cat's age`

-- FORK-15, reading B: the cat's age is information prescribed under s 15 (r 17(m)), and it
-- changes.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25(b); Cat Regulations 2012 r 17(m) (FORK-15 reading B)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, i IS AN `Information item`, d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(b), reading B -- the duty applies to` o `for` c `on a change to` i `on` d IF
        `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` d
    AND `s 3(1) -- there is a microchip database company for` c
    AND i `is an item among` `r 17 -- the information prescribed under s 15`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25; Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN d IS A `Calendar date`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`s 25 -- the last day for notice of a change on` d `given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `s 61 -- the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after` d `given the holidays` holidays

GIVEN ns IS A LIST OF `Notice`
      recipient IS A STRING
      i IS AN `Information item`
      last IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `among` ns `a notice to` recipient `of` i `was given by` last IF
    CONSIDER ns
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN n FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (    n's `in writing`
             AND n's `given to` EQUALS recipient
             AND i `is an item among` (n's `items`)
             AND `the day number of` (n's `given on`) AT MOST `the day number of` last)
        OR  `among` rest `a notice to` recipient `of` i `was given by` last

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`
      c IS A `Cat`
      i IS AN `Information item`
      d IS A `Calendar date`
      notices IS A LIST OF `Notice`
      t IS A `Calendar date`
      holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25 --` o `contravenes the section for` c `on a change to` i `on` d `, having given` notices `, on` t `given the holidays` holidays IF
        `the day number of` (`s 25 -- the last day for notice of a change on` d `given the holidays` holidays) LESS THAN `the day number of` t
    ... (    "(a)" ... `s 25(a) -- the duty applies to` o `for` c `on a change to` i `on` d
                   AND NOT `among` notices `a notice to` (`the local government with which` c `is registered on` d) `of` i `was given by` (`s 25 -- the last day for notice of a change on` d `given the holidays` holidays)
         OR  "(b)" ... `s 25(b) -- the duty applies to` o `for` c `on a change to` i `on` d
                   AND NOT `among` notices `a notice to` (`the name of the microchip database company for` c) `of` i `was given by` (`s 25 -- the last day for notice of a change on` d `given the holidays` holidays))

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 25 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 25"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 25"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(1)
GIVETH A `Kind of duty`
`s 71 -- s 25 is` MEANS `a duty to do a thing within a period or before a time`
